  "surprise": "P48 reversed: a +0.05 predictive-entropy penalty on the supervised proof tokens (sharpening; all else 081-claude) scored 363/217/400 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 433/356/422: exact means 326.67 versus 403.67, -77.0, worse on every seed (paired -70/-139/-22) and below the registered -45..+35 range (central -5). Discard. Pretraining went as predicted, and hard-target fit even improved: steps 4722/4722/4733 vs 4682/4732/4769, final val loss 0.0907/0.0903/0.0950 vs 0.0950/0.0912/0.0964 (lower on every seed, mean 0.0920 vs 0.0942), held-out greedy 0.987/0.987/0.985, totals 1029/1047/1003 s. The mechanism check failed: round-1 sample acc 0.076/0.027/0.050 vs 0.066/0.075/0.095 (higher on 1 of 3; 2 needed), round-1 targets 215/105/135 vs 187/235/306, round-4 acc 0.475/0.322/0.465 vs 0.503/0.469/0.522, RL-solved 805/581/828 vs 864/799/898 (metric_rl 738 vs 854); seed 1 was weak from round 1 and never recovered. So the softening losses (017 label smoothing, 053/054 entropy bonus, 091 softcap) do not mirror into a sharpening gain: at T=0.8 the plain cross-entropy calibration looks near-optimal, and pushing entropy either way gives a worse expert-iteration start even when val loss drops. Entropy was not logged, so how much the handed-off distribution actually sharpened is unmeasured. Infra note: the first launch lost seeds 1 and 2 to 'ssh: No route to host' during upload (pods terminated after 6 min, no harness run), so per program.md the experiment was re-run under the same NNN on all three seeds. That lost attempt's seed 0 finished ok at 430 (RL-solved 847, round-1 153 targets, acc 0.050) versus the re-run's 363 (805, 215, 0.076): identical code and seed differed by 67, so same-seed rerun noise is as large as the ~44 seed-to-seed sd, and round-1 accuracy ranked the two runs opposite to their final scores. Substituting 430 would still give a 349 mean, a discard. The lost attempt is archived under artifacts/autoresearch/previous_attempts/.",
